course: dictionary
lesson: 13548
title: Imprisonment and being kept in
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Imprisonment is a noun. It means being kept in prison, usually as a punishment for a crime. It can also mean being shut in, or not free to leave a place. Use the words around it to decide which meaning fits. «The judge gave the thief three years of imprisonment for stealing the jewels.» The judge, the court and the crime tell you it means being kept in prison as a punishment.
explain: «The storm kept the sailors in the cabin, and their imprisonment lasted two days.» No one was punished here. The sailors could not leave because of the storm, so imprisonment means being shut in and not free to go out. Always ask: what does this word mean in this sentence? Then try your meaning in the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: Imprisonment means being kept in prison as a punishment, or being shut in and not free to leave.
fact: «Life imprisonment» means being kept in prison for the rest of your life.
fact: «Sentenced to imprisonment» means a judge in a court has ordered that a person must go to prison.
fact: Nelson Mandela spent many years of imprisonment in South Africa because he opposed unfair laws.
exercise: «The judge gave the thief three years of imprisonment.» What does imprisonment mean here? | *Being kept in prison as a punishment | Being given a big prize for good behaviour | A type of school lesson | Being happy on a long holiday
exercise: What does «life imprisonment» mean? | Having a long and happy life | Living in a castle as a king | *Being kept in prison for the rest of your life | Going to prison for just one day
exercise: «The storm kept us in the cabin, and our imprisonment lasted two days.» What does imprisonment mean here? | *Being shut in and not free to leave | Being kept in prison as a punishment | Being very loud and noisy | Being sent on a trip by boat
test: Nelson Mandela spent many years of imprisonment in South Africa. What does this tell us? | *He was kept in prison for a long time | He was a famous singer who toured the world | He went on a holiday every year | He lived in a palace by the sea
test: Which phrase means being kept in prison for the rest of your life? | *life imprisonment | a short holiday | a school trip | a sunny day
exam: Choose the sentence where imprisonment means being shut in and not free to leave a place. | Maya won a prize for her painting and felt proud. | The judge ordered a year of imprisonment for the thief. | Nelson Mandela spent years of imprisonment in a cell. | *The storm kept us in the cabin, and our imprisonment lasted two days.
